cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "DemoCreate: Declarative Audio-Visual Demo Generation for Software"
abstract: >-
  DemoCreate generates audio-visual demos of software — codebase tours, website
  walkthroughs, and terminal/CLI demos — from a single declarative,
  deterministic spine. A Demo is an ordered action stream plus narration chunks,
  related to CodeVideo's virtual-IDE model and VSpeak's chunk/trigger model.
  Core outputs include silent WAVs, synthetic frames, captions, transcripts and
  a timed HTML image preview without audio playback. Byte reproducibility
  requires fixed inputs, assets, configuration and environment. Real speech,
  capture, video and PDF ingestion have explicit optional prerequisites; not
  every subsystem has an abstract adapter or a core substitute.
  Clip durations are measured from generated audio. Default word timestamps
  interpolate known text by character length; they are not acoustic word onsets.
  Kokoro is implemented; Whisper, Chatterbox and Manim remain unwired slots.
  Supplied onset annotations can be scored with explicit missing-data accounting;
  arithmetic does not verify independence or establish the absent acoustic study.
  Version 0.8.0 is a release candidate, not a published archive.
